            <ArticleTitle>Isotope scanning in the &quot;irritable hip syndrome&quot;.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>32-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A study of isotope scanning in children with irritable hip syndrome has demonstrated its role as a discriminator between Perthes disease and transient synovitis. Three children with normal radiographs had Perthes changes on scanning and went on to develop X-ray changes. An anatomical and pathological basis for the scan abnormalities is suggested.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
